  "problem": "Every ordered replay checks a shared Mutex<Option<String>>, even when the job has no error. Historical C53 stacks contain real Planner::check mutex-wait paths on both standard seeds; the latch remains unchanged through C68.",
  "implementation": "A private FirstError publishes a preconstructed String once. fail returns only after set completes; check reads the published value without acquiring the former mutex. Concurrent failures retain the first publication, later failures cannot replace it, and the final check remains after joined evaluation. No generation/RNG/cache/scheduling algorithm changes.",
